# Slope_Vertical_Impact
# Feature description: Combines Vertical_Distance_To_Hydrology with Slope_Hydrology_Impact for regions with both steep inclines and considerable vertical differences to hydrology.
# Usefulness: Highlights topography-driven hydrology impact on forest cover types, crucial for identifying unique forest zones across altitudes.
df['Slope_Vertical_Impact'] = df['Vertical_Distance_To_Hydrology'] * df['Slope_Hydrology_Impact'] / (df['Slope'] + 1)

# Combined_Wilderness_Density
# Feature description: Multiply Wilderness_Density_Depth with Wilderness_Priority and normalized Hydrology_Interaction_Impact.
# Usefulness: Integrates wilderness, hydrology, and distance density for pinpointing micro-ecological forest traits.
df['Combined_Wilderness_Density'] = (
    df['Wilderness_Density_Depth'] * df['Wilderness_Priority'] / (df['Hydrology_Interaction_Impact'] + 1)
)

# Road_Fire_Impact_Hydrology_Normalized
# Feature description: Ratio of Horizontal_Distance_To_Fire_Points and Horizontal_Distance_To_Roadways, normalized over Hydrology_Distance_Ratio.
